        "_comment_resolution": "Grid resolution set from tools/convergence_study.py's production study (output/convergence/, 2026-07-28). The old 50x50 E/z grid carried few-percent numerical systematics on the flavor ratios; 200x200 brings the E-component to ~6e-3 and the z-component to ~1.1e-2, comparable to the ~1.1e-2 fringe-aliasing floor set by n_earth_chords=50. Measured cost: ~33 s per likelihood evaluation single-core (~15x the old grid; ~10 s in the multi-core global-fit path) -- budget cores accordingly. Escalation path if the chord floor is ever addressed: the robust sub-1e-2 z knee is n_z_bins=1000 (adds ~7 s/eval via the thermal-rate grid). N_steps_MW=25 is converged to ~1e-10; n_mw_paths/n_earth_chords stay at 50 because the scan explores m_Zd regimes beyond the study's parameter points."
